It depends on the character. If I was a Wizard (who gets lots of heavy 
spell books, and has low strength) I would make one ASAP. If I was a Val 
(no spell books, high strength) I would wait until I get to a good spot.
 
> Where do you make a stash?  In the nearest box or chest?  Near a
> particular dungeon feature?  How far do you drag a chest over to
> that appropriate place?

I usually like to make them near a stair on the level where I find a box 
or chest. If I can get deep enough before I need one, I will put one 
right next to the stairs to Sokoban, because you tend to get a lot of 
stuff from Sokoban. Otherwise, the stairs near the mines are useful, as 
you also get a lot of stull from the mines.
 
> How do you make a stash?  I know that stacking a boulder on top of
> a box or a chest on top of the E-word is the best, although I
> haven't lost anything I've simply left in a big pile next to the
> stairs, either.

I use a chest or large box, or if avable an ice chest. I engrage Elbereth 
if I have a method that I don't think I'll need, but I won't kill myself 
over it. If you put the stash right next to the stairs there generally 
isn't to much of a chance for something to eat your stash.
 
> Do you make different kinds of stashes for different kinds of
